mud|v|To swallow anything liquid, for quenching thirst or other purpose; to imbibe; to receive or partake of, as if in satisfaction of thirst; as, to drink from a spring. ; To quaff exhilarating or intoxicating liquors, in merriment or feasting; to carouse; to revel; hence, to lake alcoholic liquors to excess; to be intemperate in the /se of intoxicating or spirituous liquors; to tipple. ; To swallow (a liquid); to receive, as a fluid, into the stomach; to imbibe; as, to drink milk or water. ; To take in (a liquid), in any manner; to suck up; to absorb; to imbibe. ; To take in; to receive within one, through the senses; to inhale; to hear; to see. ; To smoke, as tobacco.	o:1zs,80,2~1zs,80,2
