mzk|n|To grow dry; to become free from wetness, moisture, or juice; as, the road dries rapidly. ; To evaporate wholly; to be exhaled; -- said of moisture, or a liquid; -- sometimes with up; as, the stream dries, or dries up. ; To shrivel or wither; to lose vitality.	a:sem,10,5~sem,10,5	n:sem,10,5~sem,10,5	N:180o,73,2;1071,72,2;91q,59,12;1vb,42,5;pd9,30,1~91q,59,12;1vb,42,5;1071,72,2;180o,73,2;pd9,30,1
